; addline_overflow_beats_domain: overflow is checked before the domain.
;
; A spin sample defaults to -1, so this add leaves the i64 range entirely.
; There is no result to measure against the domain, which is why the order
; is forced rather than chosen: the domain check reads the sum, and the sum
; does not exist.
;
; Both implementations compute the checked add first and raise
; ArithmeticOverflow from it, so the precedence is a shared property rather
; than a coincidence of two orderings.

PUSH 4
SSMX r0          ; spin sample, defaults to -1

PUSH 0
PUSH -9223372036854775808   ; i64::MIN; -1 + i64::MIN has no i64 result
ADDLINE r0
HALT
